Question 4

Your organization wants to enforce that all Google Cloud resources are created using Terraform and that no one uses the Google Cloud console or gcloud CLI to create resources directly. What should you do?

A. Restrict access to the Google Cloud console using an IAM deny policy.
B. Configure an organization policy to disable all APIs that are not used by Terraform.
C. Use a combination of VPC Service Controls and Terraform to enforce resource creation workflows.
D. Use the "Essential Contacts" feature to alert administrators when resources are created outside of Terraform.

Correct answer
A. Restrict access to the Google Cloud console using an IAM deny policy.

Feedback
A: Correct. IAM deny policies allow you to explicitly deny specific permissions (such as resource creation permissions) to all users except a designated Terraform service account. This prevents direct console or gcloud resource creation while allowing Terraform automation to continue.
B: Incorrect. Disabling APIs would break all access to those services, including the Terraform automation itself.
C: Incorrect. VPC Service Controls restricts access to services from outside a defined perimeter but does not enforce that resources are created only via Terraform.
D: Incorrect. Essential Contacts sends alerts but does not prevent resources from being created manually.

