Your Cloud Run application calls a downstream API that occasionally becomes slow, causing your service to time out and return errors to users. You want to make your application more resilient to downstream API slowness. What pattern should you implement?

A. Increase the Cloud Run service timeout to allow the downstream API more time to respond.
B. Implement the Circuit Breaker pattern: stop sending requests to the downstream API when the failure rate exceeds a threshold, and return a cached or default response instead.
C. Cache all responses from the downstream API in Memorystore for Redis indefinitely.
D. Use Cloud Tasks to queue all requests to the downstream API and process them asynchronously.

