You need to run a Cloud Build pipeline that provisions infrastructure using Terraform in a target Google Cloud project. You want the Cloud Build service account to have the permissions it needs while following the principle of least privilege. What should you do?

A. Grant the Cloud Build service account the Owner role on the target project.
B. Grant the Cloud Build service account only the specific IAM roles required to create the resources defined in the Terraform configuration on the target project.
